668:
In order to provide the governing authority with accurate and current information concerning the telecommunications providers who offer or provide wireless telecommunications services within Putnam County; to assist the governing authority in enforcement of the Zoning Ordinance of Putnam County; to assist the governing authority in the collection and enforcement of any fees or charges that may be due Putnam County; and to assist the governing authority in monitoring compliance with local, state, and federal laws, all owners of telecommunications towers that offer or provide any telecommunications service within Putnam County, Georgia shall register annually with the Putnam County Planning and Development Department for a registration fee of $50.00, on forms to be provided by the Putnam County Planning and Development Department, which form shall include the following:
(1) The identity and legal status of the registrant, including any affiliates;
(2) The name, address, and telephone number of the officer, agent, or employee responsible for the accuracy of the registrant's information;
(3) A description of the telecommunications service the registrant intends to offer or provide, or is currently offering or providing, to persons, firms, businesses, or institutions within Putnam County;
(4) Information sufficient to determine whether the registrant has applied for and received any construction permit, operating license, or other approvals required by the Federal Communications Commission to provide telecommunication services or facilities within Putnam County;
(5) A narrative and map description of the applicant's existing wireless telecommunication facilities towers that are within Putnam County, including specific information about the location, height, and design of each tower. The governing authority may share such information with other applicants applying for administrative approvals or conditional use permits under this chapter or with other organizations seeking to locate antennas within the jurisdiction of Putnam County; provided, however, that the governing authority is not, by sharing such information, in any way representing or warranting that such sites are available or suitable. Any loss of use, increase in use, or change in use of existing antennas or towers must be reported at the time the change occurs;
(6) Such other information as the Putnam County Planning and Development Department or Board of Commissioners may reasonably require;
(7) Failure to register as required and to truthfully report all information required in the annual registration shall be an offense and a conviction for violation thereof shall be punished as provided in the Putnam County Code of Ordinances.
(Amend. of 6-21-2011)
